[[ ^1 ]]: Egyptian texts do not expressly state that Osiris dies, and the same is true of other gods. The Egyptians avoided direct statements about inauspicious events such as the death of a beneficial deity. Nevertheless, the myth makes it clear that Osiris is murdered, and other pieces of evidence like the appearance of divine corpses in the Duat indicate that other gods die as well. By the [[ Late Period | late-period-of-ancient-egypt ]] (c. 664–323 BC), several sites across Egypt were said to be the burial places of particular deities.

